    "name": "Static Call",
    "url": "https://php-dictionary.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index/static-call.html",
    "aliases": [],
    "description": "A static call is a call to a structure, where the name of the structure is hardcoded.\n\nA static method may be called with a static call, or with a dynamic call. Both are valid.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    class Elephpant {\n        static function trumpet() {}\n    }\n\n    new Elephpant(); // static call\n\n    $class = Elephpant::class;\n    new $class(); // dynamic call\n\n    Elephpant::trumpet(); // static call of a static method\n    $class::trumpet(); // dynamic call of a static method\n\n?>",
    "documentation": "https://www.php.net/manual/en/language.oop5.static.php",
